    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-ownership",
      "text": "01 ↗\nSTATED REASON\nThe owner moves; the mechanisms stay\n\nRequired slices of the existing DaemonPolicy replace optional numbers and local defaults. CLI composition supplies them; CL",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-resources",
      "text": "02 ↗\nSTATED REASON\nOne memory derivation feeds the whole daemon\n\nDelete the CLI’s duplicate resource-policy calculator. RSS thresholds, reports, worker heap limits, sampling, and t",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-output",
      "text": "03 ↗\nSTATED REASON\nCarry the capacity through every reader and writer\n\nCapture, disk spools, worker messages, and result codecs use the output slice. JSON and execution-control fra",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-lifecycle",
      "text": "04 ↗\nSTATED REASON\nKeep each lifetime and polling clock distinct\n\nStartup ownership, authorization, heartbeats, idle lifetime, stop escalation, signal waits, and drain acknowledgem",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-diagnostics",
      "text": "05 ↗\nSTATED REASON\nDiagnostics get their own bounded slice\n\nLog rotation, backup count, queued writes, and disconnected-trace retention use diagnostics. Trace expiry is independent",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-deadlines",
      "text": "06 ↗\nSTATED REASON\nChoose the deadline by the caller’s purpose\n\nStatus observation selects 100 ms; ordinary lifecycle and execution-status use 250 ms. Admission gets 5 s, and accep",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-recovery",
      "text": "07 ↗\nSTATED REASON\nKeep the recovery budgets nested\n\nAn accepted request gets one reattachment by default; each execute attempt gets its own fetch allowance of one. Nesting already",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-startup",
      "text": "08 ↗\nSTATED REASON\nCount startup child-failure retries separately\n\nStartup’s fixed second try becomes a policy-bounded loop. Only child exit or lost warm-up spends this budget; the",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-adapters",
      "text": "09 ↗\nSTATED REASON\nThe small-threshold seam lives in tests\n\nSeven new test helpers translate old constructor knobs into validated policy values. Tests, helpers, e2e fixtures, and t",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-tests-removed",
      "text": "10 ↗\nUNEXPLAINED REASON\nSome old test premises disappear\n\nThe CLI resource-derivation block and literal cadence assertion are deleted; central policy tests already exist in the bas",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-tests-values",
      "text": "11 ↗\nUNEXPLAINED REASON\nTest adapters also reshape the inputs\n\nSpill thresholds rise; formerly zero-inline cases write extra bytes. Helpers clamp capacities and create test output ",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-error",
      "text": "12 ↗\nUNEXPLAINED REASON\nThe reattachment loop changes which error escapes\n\nIf a reattached receipt is obtained but its completion later rejects, the new loop can report that later ",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-guard",
      "text": "13 ↗\nUNEXPLAINED REASON\nThe boundary is policed with retired names\n\nA meta-test expands a production-source denylist of old constants, optional knobs, and duplicate policy owners. ",
      "href": null,
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
